# Windows plugin breakage traces to CRLF arriving from `git clone` and turning
# every `#!/usr/bin/env python3` into an unrunnable `...python3\r`. Three closed
# upstream issues say exactly that. This is the cheapest fix there is, and it
# has to be committed before anyone clones on Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh   text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf

# The two that Windows actually runs, and that Windows shells expect CRLF in.
*.ps1  text eol=crlf
*.cmd  text eol=crlf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
